      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2017 the syndicate's gross claims outstanding were GBP 180.1m. Analysis of the gross claims development table indicates a modest net favourable prior-year development of approximately GBP 5.3m (about 2.9% of opening reserves), i.e. a release. The release reflects favourable claims development on older underwriting years together with reinsurance recoveries; 2017 itself was heavily impacted by US catastrophe activity (Harvey/Irma/Maria, California wildfires and Mexico earthquakes) which mainly affected the 2017 year of account and was largely mitigated by the reinsurance programme.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "The performance in 2017 has been impacted by the worst year for catastrophes in the US for over a decade with Hurricanes Harvey, Irma and Maria, the wildfires in California and earthquakes in Mexico causing insured market losses of $135 billion the costliest year on record (source: Munich Re).",
        "The impact of the catastrophe losses on Syndicate 1910 net of reinsurance recoveries added 18.16 percentage points to the combined ratio.",
        "The 2016 Year of Account has performed creditably given that it was affected by Hurricane Matthew and fires in Alberta, the year is forecast to be better than plan when it closes in 12 months time with a return of stamp of 11.9%.",
